2.2 Model-free Prediction and Regret
The Kalman filter in (3) requires the system matrices A and C as well as noise statistics Q and R. This is thus a model-based prediction, with its performance heavily dependent on the availability and accuracy of the system model. In this paper, we focus on model-free online learning algorithms to predict observations based only on past measurements, without requiring any knowledge of the system matrices or noise covariances. Following [12, 20], we quantify the performance of the online prediction in terms of the regret measured against the Kalman filter (3) that has full system knowledge. The goal is
