2.3 Long-term Memory and Forgetting
With (7), it is clear that the problem of model-free prediction for system (1) falls within the framework of online least squares [30]. Two recent works [11, 12] have used basic recursive auto-regression algorithms to estimate Gp and make online predictions. To reduce the dimension of Gp, [20] has embedded spectral approximation into algorithm design based on the concept of Kolmogorov width. However, the practical performance of these existing approaches can easily deteriorate due to the highly imbalanced nature of the regression model (7). Indeed, for nonexplosive systems ρ(A) ≤ 1, the state xˆk−p has a long-term memory effect and leads to a persistent bias term. A suitable past horizon length p is required to mitigate xˆk−p in (7). Since ρ(A − LC) < 1, the magnitude of each
